  "title": "Journal v2: validated events, run index, replay digest",
  "summary": "The journal grows from a single append-only buffer into a validated, indexed event store. Events now carry a typed actor, work item, change and cost; every event is checked against a JSON Schema before a byte is written; the first accepted event records the run in a per-work-item index guarded by a file lock; and a new reader replays a run, verifying each hash link and computing a replay digest over decision fields only. The buffer directory is renamed to runs, and the chain head is no longer the replay proof — the replay digest is.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
